  "content": {
    "text": "Stocks surged and oil prices fell after President Trump said on social media that he was canceling strikes on Iran planned for tonight.\nAll three major indexes finished the day more than 1.5% higher after the president said multiple countries had agreed to a deal, with the U.S. naval blockade remaining in place until the agreement was finalized. The Nasdaq composite led gains, rising around 2.5%. The Dow industrials added nearly 2%, or 930 points. The S&P 500 advanced 1.8%.\nCopyright ©2026 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. 87990cbe856818d5eddac44c7b1cdeb8",
